{#- One restic repo per minion at <repo_base>/<minion id>, on the NFS share
   that formulas/nfs-mount mounts as `mount_name` (pillar nfs_mounts). The
   run is a systemd oneshot started by a timer, as root — the NAS maps root
   on that export to its own backup user (README "NAS side").

   password — the restic repo password, required in practice — an sdb reference
   in pillar. Left blank so a missing override fails the formula instead of
   creating a repo with a guessable password. Changing it later locks the
   existing repos out (README "Changing the password").

   paths / excludes: what this minion backs up, restic --exclude patterns.
   Empty default: the formula installs everything but backs up nothing
   until pillar says what.

   stop_containers: stopped for the run and started again afterwards (by
   the unit, ExecStopPost, so also after a failed or timed-out run) — the
   apps' SQLite databases aren't safe to copy while open.

   on_calendar + randomized_delay + timeout: ends by 02:55 at the latest,
   before the 03:00–06:00 enforce window of arrstack/jellyfin
   (pillar/salt-minion-enforce-window.sls), so a repair never recreates a
   container mid-backup. A run is ~a minute; the timeout only bounds a hung
   NFS. Persistent: a run missed while the VM was off happens at the next
   boot.

   keep: restic forget --keep-<unit> <n>, applied per host after each
   backup, then --prune.

   textfile_dir: node-exporter's textfile collector directory (see
   formulas/salt-minion map.jinja) — hence the require on node-exporter.

   restore_test: a weekly second unit that proves the repo is usable —
   `restic check --read-data-subset`, a --verify restore of the latest
   snapshot into a temp dir under tmp_dir, PRAGMA integrity_check on every
   SQLite file in it. It only reads the repo, so containers keep running and
   the Sunday-morning slot may overlap the enforce window. min_free_bytes:
   headroom left in tmp_dir after the restore, else the test fails instead
   of filling the disk. #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'pkg': 'restic',
    'restic_bin': '/usr/bin/restic',
    'docker_bin': '/usr/bin/docker',
    'python': '/usr/bin/python3',
    'mount_name': 'backups',
    'repo_base': '/mnt/backups',
    'config_dir': '/etc/restic',
    'cache_dir': '/var/cache/restic',
    'password': '',
    'paths': [],
    'excludes': [],
    'stop_containers': [],
    'stop_timeout_seconds': 60,
    'keep': {'daily': 7, 'weekly': 4, 'monthly': 6},
    'retry_lock': '10m',
    'unit': 'restic-backup',
    'on_calendar': '*-*-* 02:00:00 Europe/Berlin',
    'randomized_delay': '10min',
    'timeout': '45min',
    'script': '/usr/local/sbin/restic-backup',
    'textfile_dir': '/var/lib/prometheus/node-exporter',
    'metrics_file': 'backup.prom',
    'restore_test': {
        'unit': 'restic-restore-test',
        'script': '/usr/local/sbin/restic-restore-test',
        'on_calendar': 'Sun *-*-* 04:00:00 Europe/Berlin',
        'randomized_delay': '30min',
        'timeout': '60min',
        'read_data_subset': '5%',
        'tmp_dir': '/var/tmp',
        'min_free_bytes': 2147483648,
        'metrics_file': 'restore-test.prom',
    },
} %}
{%- set backup = salt['pillar.get']('backup:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
